    "evidence_text": " It was the first single to feature lead singer Steve Hogarth, who joined the band the same year, replacing Fish.\n\nOn The West Side is the debut solo album by the Scottish folk rock artist Donnie Munro, former lead singer of the band, Runrig.\n\n Since former lead singer Donnie Munro left the band in 1997, Rory has taken lead vocal duties on songs in the band's catalogue written in the Scottish Gaelic language, as the band's new lead singer, Bruce Guthro, is not a Gaelic speaker.\n\nSteve Hogarth\n\nSteve Hogarth (born on 14 May 1956 in Kendal, Westmorland) also known as \"h\", is an English singer-songwriter and musician.\n\n Since former lead singer Donnie Munro left the band in 1997, Rory has taken lead vocal duties on songs in the band's catalogue written in the Scots Gaelic language, as the band's new lead singer, Bruce Guthro, is not a Gaelic speaker.\n\nDonnie Munro\n\nDonnie Munro (Donaidh Rothach) (born 2 August 1953) is a Scottish musician, and former lead singer of the band Runrig.",
